#82400
"Beyond a Great Archway - Magnificent Ice Cavern"
"An intricately carved mural, made of glimmering ice of wondrous, vibrant

shades of blue takes up the entire northern wall, spreading horizontally for

nearly twenty feet and roughly as tall.  The passage here runs from east to

west, ceiling arching in icy splendor high above.  The walls of the passage

are squared and smooth and made from beautiful, opaque ice, seemingly of one

unbroken layer.  From the south, where a few inches of fine, powdery snow have

collected, a dusting of the powder has blown into this cavern-like passageway,

gathering against the northern wall in soft-looking drifts.  In alarming

contrast to the pristine, undisturbed walls and fine dusting of snow, massive,

rounded tracks have been blasted into the ground, left by what looks like a

bipedal mammoth.  The passage continues both east and west from here,

perpendicular to the icy archway leading southward to the plateau.

"
"[Nereus] Entering this room should remove status0 flag in room 82416

[Nereus] ** Room Finished **

[Orb] The tracks of a bipedal mammoth?  Maybe describe instead of using that term, since I can't envision what that might look like.

[Orb] Reviewed.

[Kotoktok] line 19: \"by what looks like\" but we've never seen it. Try \"by what might have been\"

"
