#82401
"Magnificent Ice Cavern"
"This passage of smoothed, opaque ice, roughly twenty feet from wall to wall,

runs arrow-straight east to west, a beautiful cavern of ice.  A high, arching

ceiling glimmers a soft blue above, the light from outdoors softly diffusing

through the miles of ice above.  Along the floor, the otherwise pristine ice

is broken and chipped, as if dozens of extremely heavy weights have been

dropped along the surface of the ice, smashing great craters into its

surface.  A mural covers the northern wall of the passageway just east of

here, while the grand cavern also continues to the west.

"
