"Magnificent Ice Cavern - Scarred Walls"
"Walls of cloudy, blue-white ice form the north and southern walls of this

squared, arching passageway, formed from a uniform single piece of ice.  Some

great force has torn away large chunks of the otherwise perfectly smooth

walls, leaving large blocks of ice scattered across the icy floor.  The floor

as well is somewhat damaged, from the tread of some impossibly heavy creature

with nearly round feet.  The passage continues unscarred to the east, while to

the west it takes a ninety degree turn northward, deeper into the wall.

"
