"Magnificent Cavern of Ice - A Frost-choked Bend"
"The passageway bends abruptly to the east here, although it is impossible to

make out the walls or ceiling of the icy cavern because of a thick forest of

blue-white frost that engulfs the entire passageway.  Tracks along the floor

and a broad swath cut directly through the frost would suggest that whatever

creatures patrol these hallways regularly frequent this area.  It is slightly

darker and more silent here, where the rough frost that makes up the walls

gathers to muffle footfalls on the crumbling ice and blocks the diffuse blue

light visible elsewhere along this cavern passageway.  South and east from

here, the passageway clears.

