"Magnificent Ice Cavern - Overhanging Icicles"
"Once, long ago, water flowed in along the ceiling from the east, forming into

thousands of hanging icicles high overhead.  A swath of destruction cuts

through the otherwise pristine ice that makes up the cavern floor; rounded

craters the size of tree trunks have been blasted into a crude trail in the

center of the floor, tracks from some gargantuan beast.  Along the edges of

the floor where the ice is still undisturbed, tiny lumps are evident, formed

when the water dripped off from a tiny icicle high above and refroze along the

ice of the floor.  Despite the destruction evident along the floor of the

passageway, the walls have remained relatively untouched; the ice of the walls

is mirror-smooth and a cloudy, opaque blue-white in color.  The tunnel

continues to the east and west from here, stretching away in a monotony of

blue-white ice.

