#82423
"Beyond the Great Gate of Ice - Atop a Grand Staircase of Ice"
"Plunging down into eventual darkness, a steep, wide staircase leads north,

deeper into the recesses of the frozen wall.  Here, atop the stair, the floor

is made from a strangely beautiful ice.  Almost as if the tread of countless

feet has melted and refrozen the ice, the top three feet of the icy ground is

completely translucent, above a sea of opaque blue ice that descends for what

could be miles.  The walls here beyond the gate are squared away and smoothly

shaped, as if constructed out of ordinary stone.  An enormous double gate,

constructed of glittering, faceted ice occupies the entirety of the southern

wall.  Through the latticework of ice that makes up the top halves of the

gate, a narrowing passage is visible leading away through the dark ice.

"
