#82425
"Before an Obsidian Archway"
"A stark contrast to the blue-white ice of the passageway and of the wide

staircase leading up and to the south, an obsidian archway frames the

passageway leading further north.  The chamber is almost perfectly square,

with rectangular passages arranged symetrically to lead away in every

direction.  Soft piles of frost have collected in all the corners of the room,

while beneath the archway along the northern passage, frost has collected in a

deep pile, almost like a snowdrift.  The eastern and western passages lead

into rocky caverns; strange glowing runes encircle the passage almost on a

line where the ice ends and the rocky cavern begins.  The southern passage

climbs innumerable stairs up and out of these depths.  Through the shimmering

air of the arch, the passageway of flawless ice continues to the north.

"
