#82428
"Natural Cavern - Widened Passageway"
"At one point, this natural cavern passageway ran a winding course from north

to south, but it has since been widened along several points to roughly twelve

feet across.  Whoever worked the stone has done a fair job, as the walls are

relatively smooth.  It does not appear as if those responsible for widening

the tunnel had a chance to finish work on the ceiling or floor, as both are

uneven and rough; stalactites still hang from the limestone ceiling in places,

their stony twins along the ground worn away with the traffic of passing

feet.  The stone is damp with condensation, the floor covered in a thin layer

of fine, sandy sediment and an unpleasant layer of green-black, viscous

slime.  The passageway winds around a corner, leading north to west; to the

north, a gruesome pile of bones and other refuse has accumulated.

"
"[Nereus] ** Room Finished **

[Ahni] Room reviewed.

"
