#82429
"Cavern Passageway - Partially Worked Passageway"
"Abandoned in the midst of construction, this passageway has been partially

worked and reinforced with tar-soaked timbers.  A heap of unused timbers has

been neatly stacked against the southern wall, foot-thick logs of wood with

the bark stripped off and then covered in tar.  The passageway has been almost

completely finished here; the walls are smooth and at right angles to the

floor and ceiling; the passage runs straight and level, and the floor has been

flattened.  Only the ceiling with a few stalactites left unbroken has not been

finished.  The cavern passage continues to the west, where the stonework has

been finished and the tunnel is now shored up with timbers, while to the east,

a more natural cavern passageway is visible.

"
