other side, leaving rubble strewn about the cavern floor.  The stone of the

passage is fairly well worked, carved out with some kind of chisel or other

stone tools.  No rubble is evident other than that from the intersecting

tunnel to the south, so it must have been dragged away when this square

passage was first constructed.  Further west down this smoothly worked

