"Narrow Cavern Passageway - Hewn From the Stone"
"Winding abruptly from west to north here, this narrowly-cut passageway

continues to slope upward as it moves towards the north.  Narrower even than

the chute-like cavern passageway west of here, this choked passageway would be

an extremely tight fit for a horse at many points, while merely six feet high

in places.  At the narrowest points, the normally jagged rock of the walls has

been worn smooth, evidence that this region has seen a great deal of traffic. 

