"Cavernous Natural Grotto"
"A shallow pool of water, crystal-clear and ice cold, covers the rocky floor of

this naturally formed cavernous grotto.  Water trickles in slowly along the

sloping floor north of here, and also drips down from tiny stalactites growing

silently along the ceiling.  A niche has formed in the southwest end of the

cavern where the water is deepest, possibly where the water exits this

subterranean pond.  In contrast to the peace of the cool water, a cruel gash

has been ripped in the eastern wall, rending the stone apart and carving a

tunnel leading further eastward.  The grotto slopes upward to the north, the

wet stone slick and covered in sediment.

