#82445
"A Natural Grotto - Hot Springs"
"Bubbling and boiling, two deep pools running along the edges of the walls of

this chamber emit steam from their sediment-filled waters, sending steam into

passageways to the north and south.  A raised ridge of smooth, wet gray rock

is the only trail through this natural grotto, the pools on both sides too

deep and too hot to traverse safely.  The chamber is fairly large and very

elongated, running perhaps fifty feet long and twenty feet across at its

widest, while the ceiling arches overhead, probably fifteen feet above. 

Thick, sulfur-smelling steam fills the air, condensation running down the

walls and back into the boiling pools.  The steam-filled passageway curves

generally northward and southward, where what look like carved passageways

wind away.

"
