#82446
"Cavernous Passageway Hewn from the Rock"
"This slime-coated passageway has been torn from the bare rock, shaped with

claw and tooth and nail.  The excavation looks to have been mindless, without

direction or purpose; the tunnel winds sinously as it leads generally

northward, and connects east to a natural cavern.  Along the ceiling,

condensation forms rapidly, trickling down the slime-coated walls and into

jagged holes in the gray rock of the floor.  The slime and organic material

grows more prominent as one ventures east, while northward the winding passage

becomes much more steam-filled.

"
