#82447
"Cavernous Passageway - Into the Heart of the Nest"
"Thick, viscous slime drips from the walls and ceiling of this cavern

passageway.  The steamy air condenses against the gray stone walls, making the

ground slippery and dangerous to walk across.  A mat of interwoven organic

material covers sections of the floor, looking like a thick, leathery web

connecting husks of hatched egg sacs.  The gray cavern walls of this twisting

passageway appear to be purely natural; no marks are evident on the walls,

floor, or ceiling that would indicate the passage has been widened.  Between

the interwoven mats of organic material, the stone floor has been worn smooth

from erosion, due to weather or the travel of some creature or creatures.  A

larger, spherical chamber awaits to the north, while the cavernous passageway

grows even steamier to the west.

"
