#82448
"Sinister Nesting Ground"
"Discarded eggs and the almost complete organic feeling and appearance of the

walls make it immediately evident that this is the heart of this infestation. 

Originally a large, natural cavern, it has been widened in places to become a

massive spherical cavern; evidence of this expansion can be seen along the dark

grey stone of the walls, where claws have been used to dig away the rock.  In

the bowl-shaped depression in the center of the cavern, dozens of broken and

shattered eggs have collected, probably the hatching point for the entire

nest.  The dark grey rock that makes up the walls has been coated with inches

of a dark, green-black slime, which runs from the ceiling in acrid-smelling

rivulets.  The air is humid, thick, warm; it is tiring to breathe.  Escape

from this horrible place lies only south.

"
