#82449
"Beyond an Archway of Pure Obsidian"
"Knee-deep drifts of white frost have collected against the eastern and western

walls of this icy tunnel, the frost fallen from the walls and ceiling.  Even

deeper frost has collected directly beneath a great obsidian archway that

spans the entrance to this tunnel just south of here; it is clear that nothing

has travelled here in what may be centuries.  Despite the fact that the tunnel

shows no evidence of maintenance, care, or travel, the walls and ceiling are

still level and flat, opaque blue ice visible in places through the thick

white frost.  The tunnel slopes gently downward as it leads north, while to

the south through the archway a square chamber of ice can be made out.

"
"[Nereus] It's safe to just walk south through the arch

