#82450
"Downward Sloping Tunnel of Ice"
"This tunnel of ice narrows slightly as it slopes downward into the heart of

the frozen wall.  Patches of the icy walls are transparent here; beyond the

transparent sections lies either the same blue-white ice that makes up the

rest of the walls, or a dark, charcoal-gray rock surface.  Both the walls and

ceiling retain their flawless perfection here - they are as smooth as the

surface of a frozen pond.  To the north, the tunnel begins to slope downward

much more aggressively, the icy floor becoming more slippery.  Further up the

slope to the south, thick frost has accumulated along the ground, fallen from

the walls.

"
