#82451
"Downward Sloping Tunnel of Ice"
"This square tunnel of ice slopes sharply downward here, almost as if the ice

has formed atop a steep, rocky hill.  The frost-covered ceiling parallels the

sloping floor, remaining a dozen feet or so overhead.  On both sides of the

tunnel, the walls are virtually translucent, allowing a window onto another

wall of opaque ice ten feet beyond.  The effect of the transparent walls are

somewhat startling, making it look as if the walls are some trick of mirrors

or the light.  To both north and south, the slope of the tunnel is much less

noticeable and the footing appears less slippery.

"
