"Narrow Tunnel of Black Ice - Eastern Collapse"
"The tunnel ends suddenly here, collapsed by the unspeakable weight of the

thousands of feet of glacier above.  A collection of icy boulders and other

rubble has fallen, preventing travel into what might be a wider space beyond.

Unlike the blue-white, semi-translucent ice that makes up the debris, the

walls of this tunnel are far from perfect: rough, black-streaked ice comprise

the visible surfaces.  A few splotches of ancient-looking, pitted rock are

visible behind the shallow ice.  Further west, the tunnel narrows and slopes

downward, the icy rock growing darker and more pitted until it fades into

blackness.

"
"[Nereus] ** Room Finished **

