#82454
"Glittering Tunnel of Ice"
"Like the crystal clear waters of a pristine lake, the walls and high ceiling

of this tunnel of ice are made of amazingly clear ice, more than a dozen feet

in thickness.  The passageway here is artfully crafted, though completely

undecorated.  The ceiling gently arches, meeting the two perfectly smooth

walls at a gentle angle.  The floor seems to be the only permanent fixture

here - unlike the walls, it is covered in a layer of powdery frost which

somehow seems to make travel easier.  Tiny, flickering blue lights are

embedded inside the ice, glinting off and on like fireflies.  While there are

only a few visible in the ice here, further north along the tunnel there are

dozens or hundreds quietly signaling an enigmatic code.  To the south, the ice

becomes opaque; a partial collapse from the ceiling now blocks the western

section of tunnel.

"
"[Nereus] ** Room Finished **

"
