#82455
"Tunnel of White Ice"
"The ice that forms the walls and ceiling of the tunnel here is an opaque,

milky white color, except for the western wall, which is a sheet of nearly

transparent ice.  Getting traction on the slippery ground is difficult, but

the ice is not so smooth as to make walking impossible.  Several gouges have

been carved into the walls here, but appear to be shallow.  Some of the gouges

are filled with a blackish substance.  The tunnel through the ice continues to

the north and ends at a transparent wall of ice to the west.

"
"[Nereus] ** Room Finished **

