"carvings 1 east 1 south"
"The carvings seem to tell an amazingly detailed story.  A snowy landscape is

depicted, representing the plateau now thousands of feet overhead.  All along

the edges of the carved area, the jagged peaks of the Dragonspires surround

the plateau, craggy surfaces standing out starkly gray against the snow. 

Towards the northern end of the plateau, an army of sorts, made of the beasts

of the plateau, stand in front of the figure of a woman with snow-white skin,

cloaked in a bright red garment.  At the front lines of battle stand ferocious

bears, wolves with clouds of frost bursting forth from their mouths, and

enormous mammoths trumpeting their displeasure.  Their adversaries are

wicked-looking men and elves, all with scowls along their faces and wicked

grimaces visible in painstaking detail.  All along the lines of battle, dead

creatures from both sides lie still, their bright blood standing out against

the snow.  The carvings wind along the southern wall as the passage turns from

east-west to north-south, completely covering almost the entire surface of the

wall.

"
