#82458
"Glittering Tunnel of Ice"
"In contrast to the tunnel sections further west and south of here, which are

beautiful in their intricacies, this gentle turn in the tunnel is beautiful in

simplicity.  No decorations adorn the plain, purely transparent ice of the

walls and ceiling.  Within the pure, smooth, ice, tiny pinpoints of light

slowly phase on and off, glimmering a soft blue light.  Here, the shimmering

blue lights merely dot the ceiling, before miles of more opaque ice above

prevent sight of any that lie beyond.  The cavern floor could easily pass for

a beach somewhere, were it not for the cold exuding from the frost that covers

the icy ground.  The glittering tunnel through the ice continues to the west

and south.

