#82459
"Elaborately Carved, Glittering Tunnel of Ice"
"The tunnel slopes gently downward as it heads west, running in a nearly

perfectly straight line for a few dozen meters.  Along the northern wall, a

massive, elaborate carving occupies the entire wall, starting a few inches

above the frost-covered floor and stopping just before the translucent

ceiling.  Unlike the southern wall and ceiling, both of which are translucent

surfaces of ice, dotted with glimmering blue lights, the northern wall is

completely opaque, a perfectly flawless canvas for the brightly colorful dyes

applied to the carvings.  White frost covers the floor in a depth of six

