"1 north carvings"
"Like the other carvings earlier in the hallway, this one tells a detailed

tale.  Framing the entire carving are the peaks of the Dragonspires, craggy

and gray.  The plateau is a gruesome scene of death in this carving: a horde

of animals have fallen on the plain, their dark red blood staining the snow. 

Hundreds or even thousands of the evil-looking men and the occasional elf have

fallen as well, their bodies strewn across the churned-up snow.  Towards the

top of the carving, the deep, unyielding blue of the frozen wall looms; the

red cape of the witch is visible near the center of the wall at the northern

end of the plateau.  Near the figure in the red cloak, only a handful of

mighty bears remain alive and now encircle the woman, their wounds evident and

painted in vivid detail.  She has her hands raised and her mouth open as if

she is chanting, although the carving is unable to communicate what is being

said.  Further south, the army of men is in the process of regrouping, the few

tattered banners that remain held low.  Along the western side of the carving,

a gathering storm is growing, blinding snow glinting even brighter white

against the snowy backdrop.

"
