#82460
"Glittering Tunnel of Ice"
"Turning northward again as it winds like a sinuous snake through the

crystalline ice, the tunnel walls are smooth, beautifully transparent ice like

the thin skin of ice on a pure mountain pond.  Embedded in the crystalline

walls are tiny, flickering blue lights that softly pulsate, almost as if they

are alive.  The floor is covered in deep white frost which crunches underfoot.

A softly opaque ceiling arches more than twenty feet overhead, diffuse light

from miles overhead softly filtering in.  The passageway widens and grows

slightly taller to the north, the transparent ice continuing.  Further east,

an elaborate carving is visible along the northern wall of the tunnel,

covering the wall from ceiling to floor.

