covers the floor is at its deepest here, thinning to a mere covering of frost

as the tunnel slopes sharply upward to the east.  Transparent walls of ice

flank the frost-covered ground, soft blue lights oscillating between a dark

blue glimmer and a soft, steady light.  In concert, the lights seem to pulsate

in some sort of intelligent pattern.  The lights are fewer here than in the

serpentine section of the tunnel to the south, the ceiling higher, and the

depth of clear ice much more shallow.  To the east, the transparent ice

abruptly ceases, the walls the pure white of shaved ice or new-fallen snow.

