#82463
"Rock-Streaked Tunnel of Ice - South of an Icy Fissure"
"Perhaps this is finally the bottom of the ice, miles below the frigid surface

of the glacier high above, or perhaps this is just a narrow point in a natural

cavern that has since filled with ice.  Either way, this tunnel is layered,

marbled transparent ice atop opaque ice and weathered rock.  A few patches of

rock protrude through the smooth walls, worn away by passage through this

area, or water, or possibly even the movement of the glacier.  The floor here

is lightly dusted with a covering of frost, humanoid footprints disturbing the

pristine surface of the ground.  Retreat to a domed chamber of white is

possible to the south; the tunnel ends to the north where an icy ledge runs

along the top of a cold, black chasm.

