comprised of the same opaque, milk-colored ice, with the exception of the

translucent ice of the northern wall.  Behind this pure, crystal window of ice

to the north, a fast-rushing waterfall of gray-white water flows, only a faint

feeling of racing water resonating through this small passageway.  The floor

is damp and slick here and it is quite difficult to stand without falling,

although up the sloping passageway to the west it looks to be slightly easier

to gain purchase.

