"Walking on the Gray Water"
"Seemingly inches beneath your feet, a churning mass of gray water flows from

northwest to southeast and then tumbles out of sight into pitch blackness

below the corner of the tunnel.  Although the floor certainly seems solidly

frozen, it is difficult to tell exactly how thick the ice is because of the

water immediately below.  The floor is the only section of the ice that is

translucent: the walls and ceiling are a uniform, milky-opaque ice, smooth and

slick with wet.  A large, rickety gate constructed from enormous bones of all

types lies to the north, glimpses of ivory visible beyond, while the

passageway winds up and away to the west.

"
