of this snaking tunnel.  Embedded in the very walls of the chamber are several

enormous bones, some eight feet in length.  The ice of the floor is jagged and

broken, covered in the thin layer of frost that happens when ice is crushed to

fine dust repeatedly.  The snaking tunnel continues to the south, through a

poorly-constructed gate made of yellowed bone, and disappears around a corner

to the east.

