"Turning Tunnel of Ice - Window on a Waterfall"
"The walls and ceiling along this winding turn in the passageway are

interspersed with patches of translucency along the otherwise opaque, milk-

colored ice.  The patches look somehow unsettling and unwholesome, like skin

sloughing off of a leprous man.  The entirity of the eastern wall is

completely transparent, a very thin layer of clear ice.  Beyond the barrier of

ice, a sediment-filled spray of water plummets down a dark shaft and out of

sight below, the falls silent behind the clear barrier.  Unlike the smooth

tunnel walls, the icy floor has been victim of the tread of some enormous

beast; a covering of chips of ice and fine white frost dusts the ice below.

The passage starts to slope uphill to the north and west, through a crude gate

of bone which appears as if it may fall apart at any moment.

