"Icy Tunnel - A Final Gateway"
"Unlike the mottled appearance of the ice just south of here, the walls of this

section of the passage are a soft, slightly translucent, milky-white ice,

smooth and unbroken.  Twelve feet above, the ceiling is completely

transparent; above is only blackness, a shaft leading up for what could be

thousands of feet before the top of the glacier is reached.  Beneath your

feet, chips of ice and a dusting of frost have collected and crunch underfoot

with every step.  To the north lies a gate with an air of finality: a

collection of yellowed skulls watch an endless vigil, an unmistakable warning

about what lies beyond.  Escape from what lies beyond the gate is possible to

the south, where the passage turns around a corner to the west.

"
