cover the walls like the blotches on a cow, growing less frequent towards the

southern end of the passageway.  Footing is nearly impossible on the

condensation-soaked icy floor, the only completely opaque surface of the

tunnel.  To the east, the ice also slopes down before it reaches a gate made

of all manner of yellowed bones.

