west of here, a forceful jet of water which used to exit a wall of water-

smoothed rock has frozen into a slippery bridge.  Some of the water has not

frozen beneath the surface; it is still visible beneath the ice, rushing into

an alcove beneath and into unknown darkness to the east.  The western surface

of the bubble has melted away; it would be simple to cross the frozen bridge

and onto a ledge beyond to the north.  The passageway returns on an upward

slope to the north and disappears around a corner to the east.

"
!
