#82481
"Upon a Jet of Sediment-Stained Water"
"Beneath your feet churns a jet of milky-white water, which rushes forcefully

from a gap in the gray stone wall to the west.  As the water spreads out and

falls, it enters an opening beneath an icy passageway and vanishes from sight

behind the opaque ice to the east.  A frigid mist swirls langorously, chilling

tendrils working their way through the thickest clothing.  Immediately north

of where the jet of water exits the stone, a mist-filled alcove is barely

visible; it could easily be flown to from here, but it is impossible to know

what may lie ahead.

"
"[Nereus] This room can't be entered without the ice candle being lit

