"Mining Tunnel - East of an Obsidian Archway"
"Abruptly, the ice stops: a line of runes circles the square tunnel westward, a

ring of soft blue runes on wall, ceiling, and floor.  Beyond the runes to the

west, opaque ice covers the ground, while on this side of the spidery writing

there is only natural rock.  Evidently this was once a mining tunnel - old

timbers of thick, tar-soaked pine shore up the ceiling here and further along

the tunnel to the east.  A hole has been broken through the northern wall,

large enough for a human to squeeze through.  To the south lies additional

mining construction, newer than this tunnel but obviously quite old.

"
