"Mining Tunnel - Partial Collapse"
"The mining tunnel has been finished through this section, the cold stone

squared off neatly and heavy timbers placed against the rock walls.  However,

sometime after the tunnel's completion, a partial collapse has happened along

the southern wall despite the braces.  The timbers along the southern wall

have splintered, the inside of the wood mouldering in the damp cavern air.

Eight feet above along the ceiling, an ominous crack spreads northeast from

the collapsing area, innumerable tons of rock and ice hanging tenuously above.

To the east and west, the excavation continues, the passage winding abruptly

further east.

