"Ancient Catacombs"
"Ancient, pitted limestone makes up the walls of this ancient catacomb.  Even

though the ceiling is damp - water drips down from tiny, icicle-like

stalactites - the floor is worn smooth, shiny from the tread of countless feet

over the ages.  Crude niches have been carved out of both the northern and

eastern walls with some makeshift tool, clearly intended for one purpose: a

final resting place for remains.  A hole in the southern wall looks to have

been broken away with sheer force, crumbling the few inches of stone away into

a much newer passage beyond.  The catacomb extends to the west into inky

darkness.

