"Ancient Catacombs"
"The charcoal-colored limestone of the walls and ceiling is smooth and shiny,

unbroken with cracks or crevices.  There are no chisel marks evident along the

stone of the chamber; either because the catacomb was natural or because any

marks of its construction have eroded away.  A single niche has been carved

roughly from the northern wall, approximately large enough to fit a tall

humanoid.  Above and below the sepulchre, smears of blue paint can be faintly

seen.  While there is some evidence along parts of the walls that there was

