"Entrance to an Ancient Mausoleum"
"As if the living wall of sickly pink flesh to the west chokes the very air,

the bone-dry entrance to what can only be a mausoleum is stale and musty, the

scents of copper mingling with rich earth and cold stone.  The flesh is a

strange, overpowering contrast to the otherwise gray limestone of this eight

foot square chamber.  The floor of the chamber is shiny, as if endless feet

have trod the floor over ages - strange in a tomb such as this.  Charcoal-gray

slabs of limestone, darker than the surrounding walls of this entrance

chamber, seal the north, east, and southern doorways.  Sigils carved into the

very stone of the slabs somehow seems to glow black, as if they consume what

little light is in this small entryway.

