#82610
"Within the Obsidian Mausoleum"
"Deep black obsidian makes up the chamber walls, ceiling and floor, polished to

a perfect mirror smoothness.  Three columns of the same obsidian, one in the

northwestern, northeastern, and southeastern corners, leave only narrow

passageways into similar obsidian crypts to the east and north.  The southern

wall, behind the coffin placed in the center of the room, has been covered

from floor to ceiling in strange, elaborate writing.  To the west, a heavy

slab of charcoal-colored limestone seals the doorway, trapping all beyond

inside with only the dead for company.

"
"[Nereus] ** Room Finished **

"
