#82611
"Within the Obsidian Mausoleum"
"Midnight-black obsidian makes up the chamber walls, ceiling and floor,

polished to a perfect mirror smoothness.  Behind the coffin, the northern wall

is completely covered in strange, elaborate writing, etched directly into the

liquid obsidian.  A thick layer of choking dust covers the floor, unbroken by

footsteps for what must be ages.  Through the open doorway to the south lies

the empty entryway to the mausoleum; to the east, a pair of columns frame

another doorway of sorts into a nearly identical chamber.

"
