#82612
"Wards Against the Darkness"
"Like a handful of white sand tossed onto a black canvas, groupings of strange,

miniscule symbols glitter against the smooth obsidian of the floor, ceiling,

and walls.  The symbols glimmer softly, working unknown magics; perhaps to

keep the room dustless, free of damp, and prevent collapse; perhaps for some

other reason, now forgotten by time.  Contrasting with the black walls of the

tomb in texture as well as color, a rough, dark gray charcoal-colored

limestone slab seals off and prevents movement further north.  To the east,

further into the depths of the tomb, relics and treasures can be seen

throughout the small black room.

"
"[Nereus] ** Room Finished **

"
