#82613
"Within the Obsidian Mausoleum"
"Like the liquid-smooth surface of a placid cavernous sea, the walls and

ceiling of this room are smooth, black, and silent.  The obsidian surfaces are

a paradox of light; they seem to draw in light from the room and somehow

simultaneously reflect it off of every surface, making even steady sources of

light dance madly.  Like the rooms nearby, inch-high runes decorate the

entirity of the wall behind the black coffin, telling a story that only the

dead now remember.  Beyond pairs of meter-thick obsidian columns to the west

and south, contrasting gray limestone slabs can be made out, perhaps an exit

from this charnal house.  To the east, through another set of mirror-smooth

columns, the mausoleum continues.

"
"[Nereus] ** Room finished **

"
