#82614
"Within the Obsidian Mausoleum"
"Identical to the nearby chambers, the surfaces of the chambers are made up of

the same perfectly formed obsidian, polished to the same smoothness, the floor

covered in a similar layer of dust.  Unlike the previous chambers, however,

there is only a single line of spidery writing carved into the northern wall

behind the black coffin.  Also unlike the previous chamber, the writing starts

halfway down the wall, perhaps a foot above waist level of a man.  Escape from

this section of the mausoleum lies through pairs of meter-thick columns to the

south and west.

"
"[Nereus] ** Room Finished **

"
