few inches to the right of the column on the northwestern side of the room.

The neat, spidery runes are about an inch tall and stand starkly white against

the black obsidian of the wall.  Unlike the nearby chambers where the writing

covers the wall from ceiling to floor, the writing here is merely a single

line; whether because the one laid to rest here accomplished nothing during

life or their deeds could be summarized succinctly will probably be never

known.

"
