#82615
"Within the Obsidian Mausoleum"
"The mausoleum's eastward march comes to an end here, the disturbing symetry of

the burial chambers broken by a monolithic wall of obsidian to the east.  Like

the western chambers nearer the entryway, alien writing completely adorns the

southern wall, behind the unadorned ebony sarcophogus.  The same carpet of

dust obscures the polished obsidian of the floor: this place has not felt the

touch of mortal foot for many ages.  Soul-crushing, monotonous black lies

through each pair of columns: north, or west from here.

"
"[Nereus] ** Room Finished **

"
