#82616
"Within an Obsidian Tomb - Reliquary"
"A square chamber roughly ten feet across and eight feet from floor to ceiling,

the floor across the sides of the chamber is raised in odd, obelisk-like

rectangles a foot across and of varying heights.  Atop each square pillar,

some relic or trinket has been placed, some of immeasurably valuable gold,

brilliantly crafted, others mere charms.  Every surface of the chamber is as

smooth as a mirror, as beautiful and reflective as a placid black sea.  All

the surfaces, even the pillars, are covered with groups of three, six, or nine

symbols, quartz-colored and indented slightly below the surface of the black

stone.  What looks to be the final resting place of some person of great

importance lies just east through a narrow doorway, while further west there

is a small entry chamber.

"
"[Nereus] ** Room Finished **

"
